From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 20:04:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(claude-native): keep quiet sub-agents running until their
 turn ends

The forwarder reported a mirrored Claude sub-agent idle after five seconds
without new transcript records. A child running a long tool call (a build,
a test suite, a sleep) writes nothing until the tool returns, so the
Agents rail showed it idle or done while it was still working.

Before reporting idle, classify the end of the child's transcript: a
pending tool call keeps it running however long the tool takes; a turn
awaiting a model reply counts as idle only after ten quiet minutes; a
final reply, a SubagentHandback result, or an interrupt ends the turn.
The tail read grows from 64 KiB until it holds a message record and is
cached by file size and mtime, so idle polls stay cheap.

A child killed mid-tool never writes a turn end, so the server now also
settles a running mirrored child to idle (or failed) when the parent
records that child's result. Retried results are skipped so a resumed
child is not cut short.

Not upstream yet: proposed from fix/claude-native-subagent-quiet-status; drop this copy once it merges.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Docs: none (fix: sub-agent status stays accurate during long tool calls; no setting)
